''''exec /usr/bin/python3 "$0" "$@" # '''
# ^ POLYGLOT INTERPRETER GUARD (lp-11a). `bash <this file>` would otherwise interpret the python
# source as shell and EXECUTE any backticked prose in it as commands — that is precisely how the
# 2026-08-17 kill-switch wedge happened (full postmortem in mr-hold's header). Python reads this
# line as a no-op string; sh/bash re-execs the file under python3 before reaching any other line.
# Statically enforced for every python mr-* tool by mr-selfcheck.
"""mr-cost-sum — SSOT for deriving a run's own USD spend from a stream-json log.

WHAT A LOG REPORTS
------------------
`total_cost_usd` on a `"type":"result"` event is CUMULATIVE, never the cost of that one
invocation, and how far back it reaches depends on the CLI: a `--resume` invocation carries the
resumed session's counter forward (ts-3: attempt 1 ends at $59.71, attempt 2 ends at $84.41 —
the run cost $84.41, not $144.12) unless another session in the same project directory ran in
between, in which case it restarts from zero. One invocation also emits several result events
that repeat the same total. So neither summing result events nor summing per-attempt maxima
gives the spend.

Each result event also carries `model_usage_since_last_result`: per-model usage since the
previous result of the same invocation, with its own `costUSD`. That is the event's own spend
and is right whether or not the counter was carried. A run's cost is the sum of it over every
result event in the log.

A result event without that field (CLI builds that predate it) falls back to the cumulative
counter: its spend is the rise since the previous result, and the whole value when the counter
restarted — at a marker line mr-launch.sh writes before each invocation (those builds restart
the counter on `--resume`, and an escalated final attempt legitimately costs more than the one
before it, so a decrease alone would miss it) or when the value drops.

The log is not the only witness. On exit the CLI appends a `cost-state` record to the session's
transcript (`~/.claude/projects/<cwd>/<session_id>.jsonl`) whose `totalCostUSD` is the session
counter. It is written even when the invocation is killed or stopped by a rate limit before it
could emit a result event (bt-7: no result event, cost-state $64.30). Both sources can only
miss spend, never invent it, so a run's cost is the larger of the two.

A launch that continues an earlier session (mr-launch.sh's credit-stop resume) shares that
session's counter with the launch before it. Its ATTEMPT=1 marker carries `RESUME=<session id>
PRIOR=<the counter at launch>`, and the transcript figure for that launch is the session total
minus PRIOR — the earlier launch has its own cost row.

NOT USED: `modelUsage` (cumulative like the total), `"subtype":"init"` (not 1:1 with
invocations).

CONTRACT
--------
  mr-cost-sum <logfile>      -> total to 4dp on stdout, or "-" when no cost is derivable.
                                ALWAYS exits 0. Output is always /^([0-9]+\\.[0-9]{4}|-)$/
                                so callers may interpolate it into a shell or python literal.
  mr-cost-sum --run <logfile> -> one JSON object describing the build session the log holds.
                                ALWAYS exits 0:
                                  launch      UTC stamp of the ATTEMPT=1 marker, compact
                                              (20261111T123016Z), or null
                                  session_id  the CLI session id, or null
                                  model       MODEL= of the first attempt, or null
                                  escalated   an ESCALATED marker is present
                                  attempts    invocations started (ATTEMPT / COST-CAP-WRAP)
                                  unpriced    invocations that ended without a result event
                                  log_cost    spend the log's result events report, or null
                                  transcript_cost  the transcript's cost-state, or null; less
                                              session_prior for a resumed session
                                  session_prior    PRIOR of a launch that resumed this session
                                              (what it had spent before), else 0
                                  cost        the larger of the two, 4dp; null when neither
                                              source reports a cost
                                  source      "log" | "transcript" | null — which one set it
  mr-cost-sum --session <id> -> the cost-state total of that CLI session's transcript to 4dp,
                                or "-". ALWAYS exits 0. What a session has spent by now,
                                for a caller that holds its id and no log.
  mr-cost-sum --by-role <session id> [<logfile>]
                             -> one JSON object pricing each subagent of that session from
                                its own transcript. ALWAYS exits 0:
                                  session_id  as given
                                  main        the row of the session's own transcript, or null
                                  subagents   one row per <session>/subagents/agent-*.jsonl,
                                              oldest first
                                  priced      {model: USD} over every row
                                  check       with a logfile: {model: {priced, log, delta}}
                                              against the costUSD the log's result events
                                              report per model; else null
                                A row: agent_id, role (the subagent's agentType), description,
                                tool_use_id (the Agent call that spawned it), model and effort
                                (those of most of its messages), models ({model: messages}),
                                version (the CLI's), started, duration_s, calls (messages),
                                tokens {in, cw5m, cw1h, cr, out}, cost_usd (null when a model
                                is not in the rate table).
  mr-cost-sum --selftest     -> exit 0 pass, 1 fail.

  * no result event and no cost-state, unreadable or missing file -> "-" / cost null
  * >=1 result event whose spend sums to zero          -> "0.0000"  (a genuine $0 run is
                                                          distinguishable from an absent one)
  * result events with total_cost_usd absent/null/non-finite/negative are skipped.

Callers MUST treat "-" as COST-UNKNOWN. Never let "-" reach float(). An invocation killed
before its first result event contributes nothing to the log's figure, so `unpriced > 0` with
`source: "log"` means the cost is a lower bound.

MR_COST_TRANSCRIPTS names the transcript root (default ~/.claude/projects); fixtures point it
at their own excerpts.

PER-ROLE COST
-------------
A subagent's spend is in no log event: the log's per-model `costUSD` adds every subagent on
that model together. Its transcript has it. Each API message is written once per content block
under one `message.id`, and the last of them carries the message's final `usage`, so a
transcript is priced as the sum over message ids of that last usage at _RATES. Summed over a
session, the result equals the log's `costUSD` per model (fixtures/run-cost/by-role: ts-5,
opus $9.4969 and sonnet $0.5296 across twelve subagents).
"""

import glob

import json
import math
import os
import re
import sys

# Lines mr-launch.sh writes before an invocation. The first two start one; ESCALATED precedes
# the ATTEMPT line of the invocation it describes.
_INVOKE = ("ATTEMPT=", "COST-CAP-WRAP start")
_BOUNDARY = _INVOKE + ("ESCALAT",)
_SID = re.compile(r'"session_id":"([^"]+)"')


def _finite(val):
    """A usable non-negative USD figure, or None. json.loads accepts bare NaN/Infinity and
    float() accepts "Infinity"; a NaN in the ledger makes every governor comparison in
    mr-situation false, which would disable SOFT-PAUSE and HARD-STOP without a trace."""
    if val is None or isinstance(val, bool):
        return None
    try:
        val = float(val)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        return None
    if not math.isfinite(val) or val < 0:
        return None
    return val


def _own_spend(event):
    """The event's own spend from model_usage_since_last_result, or None when the field is
    absent or unusable."""
    since = event.get("model_usage_since_last_result")
    if not isinstance(since, dict):
        return None
    own = 0.0
    for usage in since.values():
        cost = _finite(usage.get("costUSD") if isinstance(usage, dict) else None)
        if cost is None:
            return None
        own += cost
    return own


def transcript_cost(session_id, root=None):
    """The session counter from the transcript's cost-state records, or None. The counter is
    restored on `--resume`, so the last record is the session total; a drop means it restarted
    and the earlier run is added."""
    if not session_id or not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-fA-F-]{8,64}", session_id):
        return None
    root = root or os.environ.get("MR_COST_TRANSCRIPTS") or os.path.expanduser("~/.claude/projects")
    total, prev = 0.0, None
    for path in glob.glob(os.path.join(glob.escape(root), "*", session_id + ".jsonl")):
        try:
            with open(path, errors="replace") as fh:
                for line in fh:
                    if "cost-state" not in line:
                        continue
                    try:
                        rec = json.loads(line)
                    except Exception:
                        continue
                    if not isinstance(rec, dict) or rec.get("type") != "cost-state":
                        continue
                    val = _finite(rec.get("totalCostUSD"))
                    if val is None:
                        continue
                    if prev is not None and val < prev:
                        total += prev
                    prev = val
        except Exception:
            continue
    if prev is None or not math.isfinite(total + prev):
        return None
    return round(total + prev, 4)


def run_of_log(path, transcripts=None):
    """Describe the build session a log holds. Never raises; see the module contract."""
    run = {"launch": None, "session_id": None, "model": None, "escalated": False,
           "attempts": 0, "unpriced": 0, "log_cost": None, "transcript_cost": None,
           "session_prior": 0, "cost": None, "source": None}
    resumed = None       # (session id, PRIOR) from the launch marker of a credit-stop resume
    total = 0.0
    saw = False
    prev = None          # last cumulative reading of the counter run in progress
    restart = True       # the next reading without its own spend starts a new counter run
    open_unpriced = False
    try:
        fh = open(path, errors="replace")
    except Exception:
        return run
    with fh:
        for line in fh:
            if line.startswith(_BOUNDARY):
                restart = True
                if line.startswith("ESCALATED"):
                    run["escalated"] = True
                if line.startswith(_INVOKE):
                    run["attempts"] += 1
                    run["unpriced"] += open_unpriced
                    open_unpriced = True
                    if run["attempts"] == 1 and line.startswith("ATTEMPT="):
                        fields = dict(f.split("=", 1) for f in line.split() if "=" in f)
                        run["model"] = fields.get("MODEL") or None
                        stamp = re.sub(r"[^0-9TZ]", "", fields.get("TS", ""))
                        run["launch"] = stamp if re.fullmatch(r"\d{8}T\d{6}Z", stamp) else None
                        if fields.get("RESUME"):
                            resumed = (fields["RESUME"], _finite(fields.get("PRIOR")))
                            if resumed[1]:
                                # a result without its own usage is read against the carried counter
                                prev, restart = resumed[1], False
                continue
            if run["session_id"] is None:
                m = _SID.search(line)
                if m:
                    run["session_id"] = m.group(1)
            if '"type":"result"' not in line:
                continue
            try:
                event = json.loads(line)
            except Exception:
                continue
            if not isinstance(event, dict) or event.get("type") != "result":
                continue
            val = _finite(event.get("total_cost_usd"))
            if val is None:
                continue
            own = _own_spend(event)
            if own is None:
                own = val if (restart or prev is None or val < prev) else val - prev
            total += own
            prev = val
            restart = False
            saw = True
            open_unpriced = False
    run["unpriced"] += open_unpriced
    # Per-event values are screened, so a non-finite total can only be float overflow across
    # events. Report unknown rather than a token no caller can parse.
    if saw and math.isfinite(total):
        run["log_cost"] = round(total, 4)
    run["transcript_cost"] = transcript_cost(run["session_id"], transcripts)
    # Only when the log's session IS the resumed one: after a failed resume the log holds a new
    # session, whose counter started at zero.
    if resumed and resumed[1] and resumed[0] == run["session_id"]:
        run["session_prior"] = resumed[1]
        if run["transcript_cost"] is not None:
            run["transcript_cost"] = round(max(0.0, run["transcript_cost"] - resumed[1]), 4)
    known = [(c, s) for c, s in ((run["log_cost"], "log"), (run["transcript_cost"], "transcript"))
             if c is not None]
    if known:
        # max() keeps the first of equals, so the log is named when the two agree.
        run["cost"], run["source"] = max(known, key=lambda cs: cs[0])
    return run


# USD per million tokens: input, 5-minute cache write, 1-hour cache write, cache read, output.
# Keyed by a substring of the model id.
_RATES = {"opus": (4.0, 5.0, 8.0, 0.2, 20.0),
          "sonnet": (2.0, 2.5, 4.0, 0.1, 10.0),
          "fable": (8.0, 10.0, 16.0, 0.2, 40.0)}
_TOKENS = ("in", "cw5m", "cw1h", "cr", "out")


def _rate(model):
    for family, rate in _RATES.items():
        if family in (model or ""):
            return rate
    return None


def _usage_tokens(usage):
    """(in, cw5m, cw1h, cr, out) of one message's usage. A usage without the per-lifetime
    split is a 5-minute write."""
    def n(obj, key):
        val = obj.get(key) if isinstance(obj, dict) else None
        return val if isinstance(val, int) and not isinstance(val, bool) and val > 0 else 0
    split = usage.get("cache_creation")
    if isinstance(split, dict) and split:
        cw5m, cw1h = n(split, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens"), n(split, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens")
    else:
        cw5m, cw1h = n(usage, "cache_creation_input_tokens"), 0
    return (n(usage, "input_tokens"), cw5m, cw1h, n(usage, "cache_read_input_tokens"),
            n(usage, "output_tokens"))


def _epoch(stamp):
    import datetime
    try:
        return datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(str(stamp).replace("Z", "+00:00")).timestamp()
    except Exception:
        return None


def role_row(path, meta=None):
    """Price one transcript. None when it holds no priced-or-unpriced model message."""
    msgs = {}            # message id -> (model, usage, effort); the last event of an id wins
    first = last = None
    version = None
    try:
        fh = open(path, errors="replace")
    except Exception:
        return None
    with fh:
        for line in fh:
            if '"assistant"' not in line:
                continue
            try:
                event = json.loads(line)
            except Exception:
                continue
            if not isinstance(event, dict) or event.get("type") != "assistant":
                continue
            msg = event.get("message")
            if not isinstance(msg, dict) or not msg.get("id") or msg.get("model") == "<synthetic>":
                continue
            usage = msg.get("usage")
            msgs[msg["id"]] = (msg.get("model"), usage if isinstance(usage, dict) else {},
                               event.get("effort"))
            version = event.get("version") or version
            stamp = event.get("timestamp")
            if stamp:
                first = first or stamp
                last = stamp
    if not msgs:
        return None
    tokens = [0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
    models, efforts, by_model = {}, {}, {}
    cost = 0.0
    for model, usage, effort in msgs.values():
        models[model] = models.get(model, 0) + 1
        efforts[effort] = efforts.get(effort, 0) + 1
        got = _usage_tokens(usage)
        tokens = [a + b for a, b in zip(tokens, got)]
        rate = _rate(model)
        if rate is None:
            cost = None
        else:
            own = sum(t * r for t, r in zip(got, rate)) / 1e6
            by_model[model] = by_model.get(model, 0.0) + own
            if cost is not None:
                cost += own
    meta = meta if isinstance(meta, dict) else {}
    t0, t1 = _epoch(first), _epoch(last)
    most = lambda counts: max(sorted(counts, key=str), key=lambda k: counts[k])
    return {"agent_id": os.path.basename(path)[:-len(".jsonl")].replace("agent-", "", 1),
            "role": meta.get("agentType"), "description": meta.get("description"),
            "tool_use_id": meta.get("toolUseId"),
            "model": most(models), "effort": most(efforts), "models": models, "version": version,
            "started": first,
            "duration_s": round(t1 - t0) if t0 is not None and t1 is not None else None,
            "calls": len(msgs), "tokens": dict(zip(_TOKENS, tokens)),
            "cost_usd": None if cost is None else round(cost, 4),
            "_by_model": by_model}


def log_model_costs(path):
    """{model: USD} the log's result events report, from model_usage_since_last_result."""
    out = {}
    try:
        fh = open(path, errors="replace")
    except Exception:
        return out
    with fh:
        for line in fh:
            if '"type":"result"' not in line and '"type": "result"' not in line:
                continue
            try:
                event = json.loads(line)
            except Exception:
                continue
            since = event.get("model_usage_since_last_result") if isinstance(event, dict) else None
            if not isinstance(since, dict):
                continue
            for model, usage in since.items():
                cost = _finite(usage.get("costUSD") if isinstance(usage, dict) else None)
                if cost is not None:
                    out[model] = out.get(model, 0.0) + cost
    return out


def by_role(session_id, log=None, root=None):
    """Price a session's own transcript and each of its subagents'. Never raises."""
    out = {"session_id": session_id, "main": None, "subagents": [], "priced": {}, "check": None}
    if not session_id or not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-fA-F-]{8,64}", session_id):
        return out
    root = root or os.environ.get("MR_COST_TRANSCRIPTS") or os.path.expanduser("~/.claude/projects")
    rows = []
    for path in glob.glob(os.path.join(glob.escape(root), "*", session_id + ".jsonl")):
        out["main"] = role_row(path) or out["main"]
    if out["main"]:
        out["main"]["agent_id"] = None
        rows.append(out["main"])
    for path in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(glob.escape(root), "*", session_id, "subagents",
                                              "agent-*.jsonl"))):
        meta = None
        try:
            with open(path[:-len(".jsonl")] + ".meta.json") as fh:
                meta = json.load(fh)
        except Exception:
            pass
        row = role_row(path, meta)
        if row:
            out["subagents"].append(row)
            rows.append(row)
    out["subagents"].sort(key=lambda r: (r["started"] or "", r["agent_id"]))
    for row in rows:
        for model, cost in row.pop("_by_model").items():
            out["priced"][model] = out["priced"].get(model, 0.0) + cost
    out["priced"] = {m: round(c, 4) for m, c in sorted(out["priced"].items())}
    if log:
        logged = log_model_costs(log)
        out["check"] = {m: {"priced": out["priced"].get(m), "log": round(logged[m], 4) if m in logged else None,
                            "delta": round(out["priced"][m] - logged[m], 4) + 0.0
                            if m in logged and m in out["priced"] else None}
                        for m in sorted(set(logged) | set(out["priced"]))}
    return out


def cost_of_log(path):
    """Return (total_float, saw_result_event). Never raises."""
    cost = run_of_log(path)["cost"]
    return (0.0, False) if cost is None else (cost, True)


def emit(path):
    total, saw = cost_of_log(path)
    sys.stdout.write("%.4f\n" % total if saw else "-\n")
    return 0


def emit_run(path):
    sys.stdout.write(json.dumps(run_of_log(path)) + "\n")
    return 0


